      </Table>
      <p>To add the parameter, click <strong>Add param</strong>, double-click the <strong>Name</strong> cell and type <code>nav-toc</code>, then double-click the <strong>value</strong> cell and type <code>full</code>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>Click <strong>Save...</strong>. The editor asks whether to write the deliverable. Click <strong>OK</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Close</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The fields have these effects:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Input map</strong> is the root map of the publication.</li>
      <li><strong>Transtype</strong> <code>html5</code> selects the HTML5 transformation.</li>
      <li><strong>Output</strong> is relative to the project root, so this deliverable builds into <code>out/full/</code>.</li>
      <li>The <code>nav-toc</code> parameter with the value <code>full</code> puts the navigation of the whole guide on each page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The editor stores deliverables in <code>project.json</code> in the project root. You do not need to edit it.</p>
      <p>The active deliverable is the one that <strong>Build Deliverables</strong> builds by default. If the status bar does not show <code>full</code>, choose <code>full</code> in the status bar's deliverable menu. You can also select the deliverable in <strong>Manage Deliverables</strong> and click <strong>Set active</strong>.</p>
      <h2 id="build-and-inspect" class="group scroll-mt-20">Build and inspect<a href="#build-and-inspect" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
